{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.q_bkm_criterion","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L62-L71","doc":"**`q`-Beale–Kato–Majda criterion** ([`thm:q-bkm-criterion`]).\n\nThe `q`-NS solution extends smoothly past `T` **iff** the\ntime-integrated `L^∞` norm of the `q`-vorticity is finite.  *Derived*\nby composing the two directional hypotheses of `QBKMContext` — the\ntheorem proves the iff (`Iff.intro`), it does not assume it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:q-bkm","label":"thm:q-bkm","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/q-bkm-criterion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.bkm_necessity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.bkm_necessity","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L60-L60","doc":"**BKM necessity (elementary direction):** smooth extension past `T`\nkeeps `‖ω_q‖_{L^∞}` bounded on the compact `[0,T]`, so its time\nintegral is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.bkm_continuation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.bkm_continuation","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L56-L56","doc":"**BKM continuation (deep direction):** a finite time-integrated\n`L^∞` vorticity norm forces smooth extension past `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.vorticityIntegralFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.vorticityIntegralFinite","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Predicate \"`∫₀^T ‖ω_q(t)‖_{L^∞} dt < ∞`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.extendsSmoothly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.extendsSmoothly","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L51-L51","doc":"Predicate \"`v` extends smoothly beyond `T`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.q","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L49-L49","doc":"The substrate parameter (generic substrate-ring element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.T","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L47-L47","doc":"The terminal time (generic substrate-ring element). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QBKMContext","kind":"class","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/q_bkm_criterion.lean#L32-L60","doc":"Hypotheses for the `q`-Beale–Kato–Majda criterion over a generic\nsubstrate ring `R` (§7c: generic `CommRing`, never `ℝ`).\n\nThe two BKM implication directions are carried as **explicit\nhypotheses** — the deep continuation direction and the elementary\nnecessity direction.  The criterion is *derived* from them in\n`q_bkm_criterion`, so the theorem is a genuine conditional result\n(\"if these directional facts hold, then the iff holds\"), the\n§3b-cond conditional-class pattern: the class axiomatises the\nconjectural inputs; the theorem derives the consequence.\n\nThe archimedean setup `0 < T`, `1 < q` are deliberately **not**\nfields: ordering is archimedean (§7c) and is unused by the iff. ","signatureChunk":0}]}